Design: I will balance the training data by using a WeightedRandomSampler to ensure each batch has a balanced representation of malignant and benign samples. I compute sample weights inversely proportional to class frequencies in the training set and replace DataLoader’s shuffle with this sampler. This helps the model learn equally from both classes despite any imbalance. The rest of the training loop, augmentations, and validation remain unchanged, and I print the best validation AUROC at the end.
