Design: We replace the BCEWithLogitsLoss with a binary Focal Loss (α=0.25, γ=2) so the model focuses more on hard‐to‐classify examples and mitigates class imbalance. We implement a FocalLoss module and use it as the training criterion, keeping the DenseNet121 backbone, balanced sampler, RandomErasing augmentation, and training hyperparameters unchanged. We then retrain for 5 epochs on the same train/val split and print out the validation AUROC.
