Design: I propose replacing the Adam optimizer with AdamW and adding a weight decay of 1e-2 to provide L2 regularization, which can improve generalization without altering the rest of the pipeline. This atomic change keeps the EfficientNet-B3 backbone, CutMix, RandomErasing, weighted sampling, TTA, and 5-fold CV unchanged, allowing us to directly measure the impact of weight decay. We then print the mean cross-validated AUROC to evaluate the improvement.
