Design: I propose integrating an Exponential Moving Average (EMA) of model parameters during training with decay=0.999. We maintain a shadow EMA model updated after each optimizer step and use the EMA model for validation and checkpointing. This atomic change does not affect the backbone, augmentations, or hyperparameters and often yields better generalization. The predict() function continues to load these EMA-based weights transparently.
